The file src/ranking.py has a bug in the function top_k. The bug is that the function does not handle the case when k is larger than the length of values. The expected correction is to add a check to ensure that k is not larger than the length of values and return the entire values list in that case.

Corrected function:

def top_k(values, k):
    if k > len(values):
        return values
    return sorted(values)[:k]
